  "content": {
    "prompts": {
      "OVERVIEW": "# DeepSeek Harness (dsh) — bundled harness\n\nSource: https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness (MIT). Modelled on release dsh-v0.2.1-alpha.2 (https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/releases/tag/dsh-v0.2.1-alpha.2), the\ndesktop release line (v0.2 ships desktop installers for macOS and Windows). Loop structure\nfrom https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/blob/master/docs/architecture.md and https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness/blob/master/docs/agent-lifecycle.md.\n\ndsh is \"everything is a plugin\" on Cordis: a profile stacks bundles (`dsh-base`, then\n`dsh-web-app` for the browser/desktop app, `dsh-headless`, `dsh-sdk-app` or `dsh-acp-app`).\nThe graph below is the turn flow of the default AgentLoop driver:\n\n1. Plan mode (optional, `/plan`): explore and design, then `exit_plan_mode` asks the user to\n   approve the plan.\n2. `agent/pre-step`: claim inbox input, assemble system-prompt sections and tool schemas;\n   `dsh-compaction-basic` relieves context pressure here (and on context-overflow errors).\n3. AgentLoop step: one model request, streamed; the assistant message is logged.\n4. Tool calls go through `tools/pre-execute` → `tools/execute` → `tools/post-execute`;\n   sensitive calls ask for one-shot user approval and fail closed without an answer.\n5. Subagents (`tool-subagent`) run delegated work in a fresh child agent.\n6. When tools owe another request or new input arrived, the loop takes another step;\n   otherwise `agent/turn-stopping` closes the turn. With `goal-round-driver` enabled an active\n   `/goal` keeps the session going in sequential Rounds.\n\nIn OHarness the step loop is folded into the AgentLoop node (the canvas graph stays acyclic).\nProviders are left unset: pick a connection (for example DeepSeek V4 Flash) in the app.\n"
    },
    "agents": {
      "agent-loop": "# AgentLoop (default driver)\n\nRun one turn as a series of steps. Each step: assemble the system prompt and tool schemas, send one model request, stream the answer, then run the tool calls it asked for. Take another step while tools owe a request or new input arrived; otherwise stop the turn. Everything model-visible is logged to the session.\n",
      "planner": "# Plan mode\n\nExplore the codebase and design the change before executing it. Keep every tool available; plan mode guides, it does not restrict. When the plan is complete call `exit_plan_mode` so the user can approve it or send you back to keep planning.\n",
      "subagent": "# Subagent\n\nYou are a child agent started by the `tool-subagent` tool. Work in your own fresh context on the delegated task only, then return a concise result. The parent received your child ID when you started and is notified when you finish.\n"
    },
    "skills": {
      "compaction": "# compaction-basic\n\nRelieve context pressure before request derivation (`agent/pre-step`) and on context-overflow errors: prune old tool results first, then summarize.\n",
      "goal": "# goal\n\nOne durable completion objective per session. Tools `get_goal`, `create_goal`, `update_goal`; humans use `/goal`. With `goal-round-driver` an active goal continues in sequential Rounds until it is completed or blocked.\n",
      "todo": "# todo\n\nKeep a short task list for the current turn with the todo tool and update it as steps complete.\n"
    },
    "hooks": {},
    "commands": {
      "compact": "Compact the session context now.",
      "goal": "Inspect or control the session goal without spending a model turn.",
      "plan": "Enter or leave plan mode."
    },
    "scripts": {}
  },
  "runtime": {
    "preferred": "api",
    "cli": null,
    "env": [],
    "secrets": []
  },
  "validation": {
    "mockProfile": "default"
  }
}
